{"id":"NCT06128629","title":"MAGNITUDE: A Phase 3 Study of NTLA-2001 in Participants With Transthyretin Amyloidosis With Cardiomyopathy (ATTR-CM)","official":"MAGNITUDE: A Phase 3, Multinational, Multicenter, Randomized, Double-Blind, Placebo-Controlled Study to Evaluate the Efficacy and Safety of NTLA-2001 in Participants With Transthyretin Amyloidosis With Cardiomyopathy (ATTR-CM)","summary":"To evaluate the efficacy and safety of a single dose of NTLA-2001 compared to placebo in participants with ATTR-CM.","conditions":["Transthyretin Amyloidosis (ATTR) With Cardiomyopathy"],"interventions":[{"type":"BIOLOGICAL","name":"NTLA-2001"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Documented diagnosis of ATTR amyloidosis with cardiomyopathy\n* Medical history of heart failure (HF)\n* Symptoms of HF are optimally managed and clinically stable within 28 days prior to administration of study intervention\n* Screening NT-proBNP, a blood marker of HF severity, greater than or equal to 600 pg/mL and less than 10,000 pg/mL\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* New York Heart Association (NYHA) Class IV HF\n* Polyneuropathy Disability score of IV (confined to wheelchair or bed)\n* Has hepatitis B, hepatitis C or human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection\n* History of active malignancy within 3 years prior to screening\n* RNA silencer therapy (patisiran, inotersen and/or eplontersen) within 12 months prior to dosing. Any prior vutrisiran use is not allowed\n* Initiation of tafamidis or acoramidis within 56 days prior to study dosing\n* Estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) \\<30 mL/min/1.73m\\^2\n* History of liver disease\n* Uncontrolled blood pressure\n* Unable or unwilling to take vitamin A supplementation for the duration of the study","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"90 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":1200,"start":"2023-12-13","pcd":"2027-12","upd":"2026-11-04","sponsor":"Intellia Therapeutics","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Trial Manager at Intellia · 1-857-285-6200 ext. 6 · medicalinformation@intelliatx.com"],"sites":[{"f":"University of Arizona","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85724","s":"STOP","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":""},{"f":"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90048","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"Western Greater Los Angeles VA Medical Center","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90073","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":""},{"f":"Stanford University","city":"Palo Alto","pr":"California","zip":"94305","s":"R","lat":37.4419,"lon":-122.143,"c":""},{"f":"University of California, San Diego (UCSD) - Medical Center","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92103","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":""},{"f":"University of Colorado Denver","city":"Denver","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"R","lat":39.7392,"lon":-104.9847,"c":""},{"f":"Yale University School of Medicine","city":"New Haven","pr":"Connecticut","zip":"06510","s":"R","lat":41.3081,"lon":-72.9282,"c":""},{"f":"MedStar Washington Hospital Center - MedStar Heart and Vascular Institute","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20010","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.0364,"c":""},{"f":"Mayo Clinic - Jacksonville","city":"Jacksonville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32224","s":"R","lat":30.3322,"lon":-81.6556,"c":""},{"f":"Cleveland Clinic of Florida","city":"Weston","pr":"Florida","zip":"33331","s":"R","lat":26.1004,"lon":-80.3998,"c":""},{"f":"Emory University School of Medicine","city":"Atlanta","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30322","s":"R","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388,"c":""},{"f":"Northwestern University","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60611","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":""},{"f":"Indiana University Health","city":"Indianapolis","pr":"Indiana","zip":"46202","s":"R","lat":39.7684,"lon":-86.158,"c":""},{"f":"University of Kentucky Gill Heart Institute","city":"Lexin